WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.192
Date columns should usually be converted from plain text into a datetime type before we analyze them.

00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:10.577
Pd dot to_datetime performs that conversion.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:17.972
Once the column is a real datetime, the dt accessor lets us extract features such as month and weekday name.

00:00:18.422 --> 00:00:27.149
For these three dates, we can immediately see which orders occurred in January or February and which weekday each date

00:00:27.149 --> 00:00:34.778
represents. Date features are useful for seasonality, reporting periods, weekday patterns, and time-based grouping.
